{
  "tema": 7248,
  "slug": "le-gusta-nos-gusta-les-gusta",
  "titulo": "Gustar with he, she, we, they",
  "subtitulo": "Le gusta el mar. Nos gustan las olas.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "To say what he, she, you (usted), we or they like, use le, nos or les + gusta (one thing or an infinitive) or gustan (several things). The thing liked is the subject; the person is the indirect pronoun.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Gustar** works backwards: the thing **pleases** the person. The person is a short pronoun:"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "Pronoun",
            "One thing",
            "Several things"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "le",
              "le gusta",
              "le gustan"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "nos",
              "nos gusta",
              "nos gustan"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "les",
              "les gusta",
              "les gustan"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Gusta** for one thing or an action: **Le gusta el café.** **Nos gusta surfear.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Gustan** for several things: **Les gustan los perros.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Le** can mean him, her or you (usted); **les** can mean them or you all. To make it clear, add **a él**, **a ella**, **a usted**, **a ellos**, **a ustedes** or a name: **A Juan le gusta.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Negative: **no** goes before the pronoun: **No nos gusta el frío.**"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: look at the thing, not the person. The thing decides **gusta** or **gustan**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Le gusta== mucho el jiu-jitsu.",
              "en": "He really likes jiu-jitsu."
            },
            {
              "es": "A mi mamá ==le gustan== las suculentas.",
              "en": "My mom likes succulents."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Nos gusta== surfear temprano.",
              "en": "We like to surf early."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Nos gustan== los tacos de pescado.",
              "en": "We like fish tacos."
            },
            {
              "es": "A mis amigos ==les gusta== The Expanse.",
              "en": "My friends like The Expanse."
            },
            {
              "es": "¿==Les gustan== los chiles toreados?",
              "en": "Do you all like blistered chiles?"
            },
            {
              "es": "A ella no ==le gusta== el ruido.",
              "en": "She doesn't like noise."
            },
            {
              "es": "Señor, ¿==le gusta== la habitación?",
              "en": "Sir, do you like the room?"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "pares",
          "lista": [
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Él gusta el café."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "A él le gusta el café."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The person is **le**, not the subject."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Les gusta los tacos."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Les gustan los tacos."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Plural thing → **gustan**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Nos gustamos la playa."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "Nos gusta la playa."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "The verb agrees with **la playa**."
            },
            {
              "filas": [
                {
                  "v": "mal",
                  "t": "Mis papás les gusta bailar."
                },
                {
                  "v": "bien",
                  "t": "A mis papás les gusta bailar."
                }
              ],
              "nota": "Add **a** before the person."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
